	</div>
</div></div></div></div></section><div class="vc_row-full-width vc_clearfix"></div><section class="vc_section vc_custom_1770671369969 vc_section-has-fill"><div class="vc_row wpb_row vc_row-fluid vc_custom_1778693426545"><div class="wpb_column vc_column_container vc_col-sm-12"><div class="vc_column-inner"><div class="wpb_wrapper"><h2 style="font-size: 40px;color: #002D5D;text-align: left;font-family:Open Sans;font-weight:400;font-style:normal" class="vc_custom_heading vc_do_custom_heading vc_custom_1781534176667" >Active Governance and Advisory Board Volunteer Opportunities</h2>
	<div class="wpb_text_column wpb_content_element  vc_custom_1783715972645" >
		<div class="wpb_wrapper">
			<p>The El Paso County Volunteer Program is a wonderful opportunity for citizens to learn about the various functions of county government as well as give back to the community. The County’s numerous boards and commissions need your experience, talents, and time.</p>
<p> </p>

		</div>
	</div>

	<div class="wpb_text_column wpb_content_element " >
		<div class="wpb_wrapper">
			<p><strong><span style="color: #002d5d">Governance Board</span></strong><br />
A governance board is an official, legally established body with decision-making authority over operations and policy. This may include voting to adopt a budget or hiring and overseeing a senior executive.</p>
<p><strong><span style="color: #002d5d">Advisory Board</span></strong><br />
An advisory board is a formally or informally created group that provides recommendations to the governance board or staff but does not have authority to act. This can include gathering community input or offering technical expertise.</p>

		</div>
	</div>
</div></div></div></div><div class="vc_row wpb_row vc_row-fluid vc_custom_1781538054180"><div class="wpb_column vc_column_container vc_col-sm-12"><div class="vc_column-inner"><div class="wpb_wrapper"><h3 style="font-size: 30px;color: #002D5D;text-align: left;font-family:Open Sans;font-weight:400;font-style:normal" class="vc_custom_heading vc_do_custom_heading" >Active Governance Boards</h3></div></div></div></div><div class="vc_row wpb_row vc_row-fluid vc_custom_1781538175713 vc_row-has-fill vc_column-gap-30"><div class="wpb_column vc_column_container vc_col-sm-6 vc_col-has-fill"><div class="vc_column-inner vc_custom_1770674435925"><div class="wpb_wrapper"><div class="ult_exp_section_layer ult-adjust-bottom-margin  " >
		<div id="uvc-exp-wrap-2630" role="button" tabindex="0" aria-pressed="false"  data-ultimate-target='#uvc-exp-wrap-2630'  data-responsive-json-new='{"font-size":"desktop:20px;","line-height":"desktop:20px;"}'  class="ult_exp_section  ult-responsive " style="color:#333333;background-color:#dbdbdb; font-weight:normal;  text-align:center;" data-textcolor="#333333"data-texthover="#333333"data-icncolor="#333333"data-ihover="#333333"data-height="0"data-cntbg="#dbdbdb"data-cnthvrbg="#e5e5e5"data-headerbg="#dbdbdb"data-headerhover="#e5e5e5"data-title="911 Emergency Response Center Authority Board"data-newtitle="911 Emergency Response Center Authority Board"data-icon=""data-newicon=""data-activeicon="#333333"data-effect="slideToggle"data-override="0"data-activetitle="#333333"data-activebg="#dbdbdb"data-img=""data-newimg=""><div  class="ult_exp_section-main ">
					<div class="ult_expheader" >911 Emergency Response Center Authority Board
					 </div></div>
				</div><div class="ult_exp_content " style="background-color:#dbdbdb;  "><div class="ult_ecpsub_cont" style=" " ><section class="vc_cta3-container"><div class="vc_general vc_do_cta3 vc_cta3 vc_cta3-style-classic vc_cta3-shape-rounded vc_cta3-align-left vc_cta3-color-classic vc_cta3-icon-size-md vc_cta3-actions-bottom vc_custom_1775576746096"><div class="vc_cta3_content-container"><div class="vc_cta3-content"><header class="vc_cta3-content-header"></header><p>The El Paso / Teller County 911 Authority Board was established as a separate governmental entity in 1990. Two counties, 11 cities, three military installations and 23 fire protection districts have signed the intergovernmental agreement creating the Authority Board. This board is the governing body responsible for the organization, administration and operation of the emergency telephone system (911).</p>
</div><div class="vc_cta3-actions"><div class="vc_btn3-container vc_btn3-inline" ><a class="vc_general vc_btn3 vc_btn3-size-md vc_btn3-shape-rounded vc_btn3-style-modern vc_btn3-color-grey" href="https://bocc.elpasoco.com/volunteer/911-emergency-response-center-authority-board/" title="911 ERC Authority Board">More on 911 ERC Authority Board</a></div></div></div></div></section></div></div>

			</div><div class="ult_exp_section_layer ult-adjust-bottom-margin  " >
		<div id="uvc-exp-wrap-6360" role="button" tabindex="0" aria-pressed="false"  data-ultimate-target='#uvc-exp-wrap-6360'  data-responsive-json-new='{"font-size":"desktop:20px;","line-height":"desktop:20px;"}'  class="ult_exp_section  ult-responsive " style="color:#333333;background-color:#dbdbdb; font-weight:normal;  text-align:center;" data-textcolor="#333333"data-texthover="#333333"data-icncolor="#333333"data-ihover="#333333"data-height="0"data-cntbg="#dbdbdb"data-cnthvrbg="#e5e5e5"data-headerbg="#dbdbdb"data-headerhover="#e5e5e5"data-title="Board of Health"data-newtitle="Board of Health"data-icon=""data-newicon=""data-activeicon="#333333"data-effect="slideToggle"data-override="0"data-activetitle="#333333"data-activebg="#dbdbdb"data-img=""data-newimg=""><div  class="ult_exp_section-main ">
					<div class="ult_expheader" >Board of Health
					 </div></div>
				</div><div class="ult_exp_content " style="background-color:#dbdbdb;  "><div class="ult_ecpsub_cont" style=" " ><section class="vc_cta3-container"><div class="vc_general vc_do_cta3 vc_cta3 vc_cta3-style-classic vc_cta3-shape-rounded vc_cta3-align-left vc_cta3-color-classic vc_cta3-icon-size-md vc_cta3-actions-bottom vc_custom_1781884974954"><div class="vc_cta3_content-container"><div class="vc_cta3-content"><header class="vc_cta3-content-header"></header><p><span style="color: #002d5d">The El Paso County Board of Health is the governing body for El Paso County Public Health. The Board of Health is responsible for developing public health policies, approving a local public health improvement plan, providing advice to the Public Health Director, and overseeing Public Health financial matters, among other responsibilities.</span></p>
</div><div class="vc_cta3-actions"><div class="vc_btn3-container vc_btn3-inline" ><a class="vc_general vc_btn3 vc_btn3-size-md vc_btn3-shape-rounded vc_btn3-style-modern vc_btn3-color-grey" href="https://bocc.elpasoco.com/volunteer/board-of-health/" title="Board of Health Information">More about the Board of Health</a></div></div></div></div></section></div></div>

			</div><div class="ult_exp_section_layer ult-adjust-bottom-margin  " >
		<div id="uvc-exp-wrap-7891" role="button" tabindex="0" aria-pressed="false"  data-ultimate-target='#uvc-exp-wrap-7891'  data-responsive-json-new='{"font-size":"desktop:20px;","line-height":"desktop:20px;"}'  class="ult_exp_section  ult-responsive " style="color:#333333;background-color:#dbdbdb; font-weight:normal;  text-align:center;" data-textcolor="#333333"data-texthover="#333333"data-icncolor="#333333"data-ihover="#333333"data-height="0"data-cntbg="#dbdbdb"data-cnthvrbg="#e5e5e5"data-headerbg="#dbdbdb"data-headerhover="#e5e5e5"data-title="Board of Retirement"data-newtitle="Board of Retirement"data-icon=""data-newicon=""data-activeicon="#333333"data-effect="slideToggle"data-override="0"data-activetitle="#333333"data-activebg="#dbdbdb"data-img=""data-newimg=""><div  class="ult_exp_section-main ">
					<div class="ult_expheader" >Board of Retirement
					 </div></div>
				</div><div class="ult_exp_content " style="background-color:#dbdbdb;  "><div class="ult_ecpsub_cont" style=" " ><section class="vc_cta3-container"><div class="vc_general vc_do_cta3 vc_cta3 vc_cta3-style-classic vc_cta3-shape-rounded vc_cta3-align-left vc_cta3-color-classic vc_cta3-icon-size-md vc_cta3-actions-bottom vc_custom_1781886052472"><div class="vc_cta3_content-container"><div class="vc_cta3-content"><header class="vc_cta3-content-header"></header><p><span style="color: #002d5d">The purpose of the Board of Retirement is to oversee the retirement plan and manage all matters related to its administration. This includes supervising the plan’s operations, setting policies, ensuring compliance with applicable laws and regulations, and acting in the best interests of plan members and beneficiaries. The Board is responsible for the overall governance and management of the Plan.</span></p>
</div><div class="vc_cta3-actions"><div class="vc_btn3-container vc_btn3-inline" ><a class="vc_general vc_btn3 vc_btn3-size-md vc_btn3-shape-rounded vc_btn3-style-modern vc_btn3-color-grey" href="http://bocc.elpasoco.com/volunteer/board-of-retirement/" title="Board of Retirement">More about the Board of Retirement</a></div></div></div></div></section></div></div>

			</div><div class="ult_exp_section_layer ult-adjust-bottom-margin  " >
		<div id="uvc-exp-wrap-9997" role="button" tabindex="0" aria-pressed="false"  data-ultimate-target='#uvc-exp-wrap-9997'  data-responsive-json-new='{"font-size":"desktop:20px;","line-height":"desktop:20px;"}'  class="ult_exp_section  ult-responsive " style="color:#333333;background-color:#dbdbdb; font-weight:normal;  text-align:center;" data-textcolor="#333333"data-texthover="#333333"data-icncolor="#333333"data-ihover="#333333"data-height="0"data-cntbg="#dbdbdb"data-cnthvrbg="#e5e5e5"data-headerbg="#dbdbdb"data-headerhover="#e5e5e5"data-title="Community Corrections Board"data-newtitle="Community Corrections Board"data-icon=""data-newicon=""data-activeicon="#333333"data-effect="slideToggle"data-override="0"data-activetitle="#333333"data-activebg="#dbdbdb"data-img=""data-newimg=""><div  class="ult_exp_section-main ">
					<div class="ult_expheader" >Community Corrections Board
					 </div></div>
				</div><div class="ult_exp_content " style="background-color:#dbdbdb;  "><div class="ult_ecpsub_cont" style=" " ><section class="vc_cta3-container"><div class="vc_general vc_do_cta3 vc_cta3 vc_cta3-style-classic vc_cta3-shape-rounded vc_cta3-align-left vc_cta3-color-classic vc_cta3-icon-size-md vc_cta3-actions-bottom vc_custom_1781886076256"><div class="vc_cta3_content-container"><div class="vc_cta3-content"><header class="vc_cta3-content-header"></header><p><span style="color: #002d5d">The Community Corrections Board determines which offenders can safely be placed in the community, who can operate a community corrections program; under what conditions an offender can participate in a program, and the standards by which a service provider can operate a facility. The board also monitors programs in the Fourth Judicial District, oversees compliance with state and local standards, recommends contracts and reception of grants, and advises the El Paso County Board of Commissioners on work release and other community corrections matters in the Fourth Judicial District.</span></p>
</div><div class="vc_cta3-actions"><div class="vc_btn3-container vc_btn3-inline" ><a class="vc_general vc_btn3 vc_btn3-size-md vc_btn3-shape-rounded vc_btn3-style-modern vc_btn3-color-grey" href="http://bocc.elpasoco.com/volunteer/community-corrections-board/" title="Community Corrections Board">More about Community Corrections Board</a></div></div></div></div></section></div></div>

			</div><div class="ult_exp_section_layer ult-adjust-bottom-margin  " >
		<div id="uvc-exp-wrap-5535" role="button" tabindex="0" aria-pressed="false"  data-ultimate-target='#uvc-exp-wrap-5535'  data-responsive-json-new='{"font-size":"desktop:20px;","line-height":"desktop:20px;"}'  class="ult_exp_section  ult-responsive " style="color:#333333;background-color:#dbdbdb; font-weight:normal;  text-align:center;" data-textcolor="#333333"data-texthover="#333333"data-icncolor="#333333"data-ihover="#333333"data-height="0"data-cntbg="#dbdbdb"data-cnthvrbg="#e5e5e5"data-headerbg="#dbdbdb"data-headerhover="#e5e5e5"data-title="El Paso County Fairgrounds Corporation"data-newtitle="El Paso County Fairgrounds Corporation"data-icon=""data-newicon=""data-activeicon="#333333"data-effect="slideToggle"data-override="0"data-activetitle="#333333"data-activebg="#dbdbdb"data-img=""data-newimg=""><div  class="ult_exp_section-main ">
					<div class="ult_expheader" >El Paso County Fairgrounds Corporation
					 </div></div>
				</div><div class="ult_exp_content " style="background-color:#dbdbdb;  "><div class="ult_ecpsub_cont" style=" " ><section class="vc_cta3-container"><div class="vc_general vc_do_cta3 vc_cta3 vc_cta3-style-classic vc_cta3-shape-rounded vc_cta3-align-left vc_cta3-color-classic vc_cta3-icon-size-md vc_cta3-actions-bottom vc_custom_1781886089420"><div class="vc_cta3_content-container"><div class="vc_cta3-content"><header class="vc_cta3-content-header"></header><p><span style="color: #002d5d">The Fairgrounds Corporation is a non-profit corporation established by the Board of El Paso County Commissioners to acquire, manage, and/or hold a liquor license assigned to the El Paso County Fairgrounds, to coordinate the use of the Fairgrounds for special events that desire consumption of alcohol, including racing events and other large special events; and through its operation, to provide funding to support the El Paso County Fair, El Paso County Fair and Events Center, and El Paso County 4H program.</span></p>
</div><div class="vc_cta3-actions"><div class="vc_btn3-container vc_btn3-inline" ><a class="vc_general vc_btn3 vc_btn3-size-md vc_btn3-shape-rounded vc_btn3-style-modern vc_btn3-color-grey" href="http://bocc.elpasoco.com/volunteer/fairgrounds-corporation/" title="Fairgrounds Corporation">Fairgrounds Corporation</a></div></div></div></div></section></div></div>

			</div></div></div></div><div class="wpb_column vc_column_container vc_col-sm-6 vc_col-has-fill"><div class="vc_column-inner vc_custom_1770670428035"><div class="wpb_wrapper"><div class="ult_exp_section_layer ult-adjust-bottom-margin  " >
		<div id="uvc-exp-wrap-4505" role="button" tabindex="0" aria-pressed="false"  data-ultimate-target='#uvc-exp-wrap-4505'  data-responsive-json-new='{"font-size":"desktop:20px;","line-height":"desktop:20px;"}'  class="ult_exp_section  ult-responsive " style="color:#333333;background-color:#dbdbdb; font-weight:normal;  text-align:center;" data-textcolor="#333333"data-texthover="#333333"data-icncolor="#333333"data-ihover="#333333"data-height="0"data-cntbg="#dbdbdb"data-cnthvrbg="#e5e5e5"data-headerbg="#dbdbdb"data-headerhover="#e5e5e5"data-title="El Paso County Housing Authority"data-newtitle="El Paso County Housing Authority"data-icon=""data-newicon=""data-activeicon="#333333"data-effect="slideToggle"data-override="0"data-activetitle="#333333"data-activebg="#dbdbdb"data-img=""data-newimg=""><div  class="ult_exp_section-main ">
					<div class="ult_expheader" >El Paso County Housing Authority
					 </div></div>
				</div><div class="ult_exp_content " style="background-color:#dbdbdb;  "><div class="ult_ecpsub_cont" style=" " ><section class="vc_cta3-container"><div class="vc_general vc_do_cta3 vc_cta3 vc_cta3-style-classic vc_cta3-shape-rounded vc_cta3-align-left vc_cta3-color-classic vc_cta3-icon-size-md vc_cta3-actions-bottom vc_custom_1781886152740"><div class="vc_cta3_content-container"><div class="vc_cta3-content"><header class="vc_cta3-content-header"></header><p><span style="color: #002d5d">The El Paso County Housing Authority was established to help promote the availability of decent, safe, and affordable dwelling accommodations in the county for persons of low-to-moderate income. The Housing Authority advises the Board of County Commissioners on matters regarding the issuance of bonds for the acquisition, construction, and rehabilitation of single and multi-family residential housing to provide more affordable housing opportunities for residents. In addition, the Housing Authority manages the Housing Trust Fund, which was established to provide funding to agencies with experience in the design and administration of innovative programs that address local housing needs.</span></p>
</div><div class="vc_cta3-actions"><div class="vc_btn3-container vc_btn3-inline" ><a class="vc_general vc_btn3 vc_btn3-size-md vc_btn3-shape-rounded vc_btn3-style-modern vc_btn3-color-grey" href="http://bocc.elpasoco.com/volunteer/el-paso-county-housing-authority/" title="El Paso County Housing Authority">El Paso County Housing Authority</a></div></div></div></div></section></div></div>

			</div><div class="ult_exp_section_layer ult-adjust-bottom-margin  " >
		<div id="uvc-exp-wrap-9387" role="button" tabindex="0" aria-pressed="false"  data-ultimate-target='#uvc-exp-wrap-9387'  data-responsive-json-new='{"font-size":"desktop:20px;","line-height":"desktop:20px;"}'  class="ult_exp_section  ult-responsive " style="color:#333333;background-color:#dbdbdb; font-weight:normal;  text-align:center;" data-textcolor="#333333"data-texthover="#333333"data-icncolor="#333333"data-ihover="#333333"data-height="0"data-cntbg="#dbdbdb"data-cnthvrbg="#e5e5e5"data-headerbg="#dbdbdb"data-headerhover="#e5e5e5"data-title="Facilities Corporation"data-newtitle="Facilities Corporation"data-icon=""data-newicon=""data-activeicon="#333333"data-effect="slideToggle"data-override="0"data-activetitle="#333333"data-activebg="#dbdbdb"data-img=""data-newimg=""><div  class="ult_exp_section-main ">
					<div class="ult_expheader" >Facilities Corporation
					 </div></div>
				</div><div class="ult_exp_content " style="background-color:#dbdbdb;  "><div class="ult_ecpsub_cont" style=" " ><section class="vc_cta3-container"><div class="vc_general vc_do_cta3 vc_cta3 vc_cta3-style-classic vc_cta3-shape-rounded vc_cta3-align-left vc_cta3-color-classic vc_cta3-icon-size-md vc_cta3-actions-bottom vc_custom_1781886141384"><div class="vc_cta3_content-container"><div class="vc_cta3-content"><header class="vc_cta3-content-header"></header><p><span style="color: #002d5d">The El Paso County Facilities Corporation, a Colorado Nonprofit Corporation, was established in 1995 to purchase, lease or otherwise acquire real estate and personal property (facilities) within the boundaries of El Paso County for the use and benefit of the county utilizing the certificates of participation (COPs) funding instrument.</span></p>
</div><div class="vc_cta3-actions"><div class="vc_btn3-container vc_btn3-inline" ><a class="vc_general vc_btn3 vc_btn3-size-md vc_btn3-shape-rounded vc_btn3-style-modern vc_btn3-color-grey" href="https://bocc.elpasoco.com/volunteer/facilities-corporation/" title="Facilities Corporation">Facilities Corporation</a></div></div></div></div></section></div></div>

			</div><div class="ult_exp_section_layer ult-adjust-bottom-margin  " >
		<div id="uvc-exp-wrap-9954" role="button" tabindex="0" aria-pressed="false"  data-ultimate-target='#uvc-exp-wrap-9954'  data-responsive-json-new='{"font-size":"desktop:20px;","line-height":"desktop:20px;"}'  class="ult_exp_section  ult-responsive " style="color:#333333;background-color:#dbdbdb; font-weight:normal;  text-align:center;" data-textcolor="#333333"data-texthover="#333333"data-icncolor="#333333"data-ihover="#333333"data-height="0"data-cntbg="#dbdbdb"data-cnthvrbg="#e5e5e5"data-headerbg="#dbdbdb"data-headerhover="#e5e5e5"data-title="Pikes Peak Library District Board"data-newtitle="Pikes Peak Library District Board"data-icon=""data-newicon=""data-activeicon="#333333"data-effect="slideToggle"data-override="0"data-activetitle="#333333"data-activebg="#dbdbdb"data-img=""data-newimg=""><div  class="ult_exp_section-main ">
					<div class="ult_expheader" >Pikes Peak Library District Board
					 </div></div>
				</div><div class="ult_exp_content " style="background-color:#dbdbdb;  "><div class="ult_ecpsub_cont" style=" " ><section class="vc_cta3-container"><div class="vc_general vc_do_cta3 vc_cta3 vc_cta3-style-classic vc_cta3-shape-rounded vc_cta3-align-left vc_cta3-color-classic vc_cta3-icon-size-md vc_cta3-actions-bottom vc_custom_1781886126721"><div class="vc_cta3_content-container"><div class="vc_cta3-content"><header class="vc_cta3-content-header"></header><p><span style="color: #002d5d">The Pikes Peak Library District Board of Trustees acts as the governing body of the library. Its responsibilities include, but are not limited to, setting policy, which is responsive and appropriate for the operation of the library district, hiring the director, evaluating the director, and approving the annual budget.</span></p>
</div><div class="vc_cta3-actions"><div class="vc_btn3-container vc_btn3-inline" ><a class="vc_general vc_btn3 vc_btn3-size-md vc_btn3-shape-rounded vc_btn3-style-modern vc_btn3-color-grey" href="http://bocc.elpasoco.com/volunteer/pikes-peak-library-district-board/" title="Pikes Peak Library District Board of Trustees">Learn more about the PPLD Board of Trustees</a></div></div></div></div></section></div></div>

			</div><div class="ult_exp_section_layer ult-adjust-bottom-margin  " >
		<div id="uvc-exp-wrap-2448" role="button" tabindex="0" aria-pressed="false"  data-ultimate-target='#uvc-exp-wrap-2448'  data-responsive-json-new='{"font-size":"desktop:20px;","line-height":"desktop:20px;"}'  class="ult_exp_section  ult-responsive " style="color:#333333;background-color:#dbdbdb; font-weight:normal;  text-align:center;" data-textcolor="#333333"data-texthover="#333333"data-icncolor="#333333"data-ihover="#333333"data-height="0"data-cntbg="#dbdbdb"data-cnthvrbg="#e5e5e5"data-headerbg="#dbdbdb"data-headerhover="#e5e5e5"data-title="Joint Initiatives Reach Committee"data-newtitle="Joint Initiatives Reach Committee"data-icon=""data-newicon=""data-activeicon="#333333"data-effect="slideToggle"data-override="0"data-activetitle="#333333"data-activebg="#dbdbdb"data-img=""data-newimg=""><div  class="ult_exp_section-main ">
					<div class="ult_expheader" >Joint Initiatives Reach Committee
					 </div></div>
				</div><div class="ult_exp_content " style="background-color:#dbdbdb;  "><div class="ult_ecpsub_cont" style=" " ><section class="vc_cta3-container"><div class="vc_general vc_do_cta3 vc_cta3 vc_cta3-style-classic vc_cta3-shape-rounded vc_cta3-align-left vc_cta3-color-classic vc_cta3-icon-size-md vc_cta3-actions-bottom vc_custom_1781886115719"><div class="vc_cta3_content-container"><div class="vc_cta3-content"><header class="vc_cta3-content-header"></header><p><span style="color: #002d5d">El Paso County is one of more than 40 counties in Colorado which participates in the House Bill 04-1451 Collaborative Management Program (CMP). This statute recognizes the need for a collective community approach to serving children/youth with complex needs through a tailored integrated approach and with child, youth and family engagement in planning, services, and solutions. The work of the initiative is funded through statutory incentive funds and grants, and its purpose is to:</span></p>
<ol>
<li><span style="color: #002d5d">Reduce duplication and eliminate fragmentation of services provided to children, youth and families who would benefit from integrated multi-agency services.</span></li>
<li><span style="color: #002d5d">Increase the quality, appropriateness, and effectiveness of services delivered to children and families who would benefit from multi-agency services, to achieve better outcomes;</span></li>
<li><span style="color: #002d5d">Encourage cost sharing among service providers.</span></li>
</ol>
</div><div class="vc_cta3-actions"><div class="vc_btn3-container vc_btn3-inline" ><a class="vc_general vc_btn3 vc_btn3-size-md vc_btn3-shape-rounded vc_btn3-style-modern vc_btn3-color-grey" href="https://bocc.elpasoco.com/volunteer/joint-initiatives-reach-committee/" title="Joint Initiatives Reach Committee">Learn more about the Joint Initiatives Reach Committee</a></div></div></div></div></section></div></div>

			</div><div class="ult_exp_section_layer ult-adjust-bottom-margin  " >
		<div id="uvc-exp-wrap-9368" role="button" tabindex="0" aria-pressed="false"  data-ultimate-target='#uvc-exp-wrap-9368'  data-responsive-json-new='{"font-size":"desktop:20px;","line-height":"desktop:20px;"}'  class="ult_exp_section  ult-responsive " style="color:#333333;background-color:#dbdbdb; font-weight:normal;  text-align:center;" data-textcolor="#333333"data-texthover="#333333"data-icncolor="#333333"data-ihover="#333333"data-height="0"data-cntbg="#dbdbdb"data-cnthvrbg="#e5e5e5"data-headerbg="#dbdbdb"data-headerhover="#e5e5e5"data-title="Pikes Peak Regional Building Department Board of Review"data-newtitle="Pikes Peak Regional Building Department Board of Review"data-icon=""data-newicon=""data-activeicon="#333333"data-effect="slideToggle"data-override="0"data-activetitle="#333333"data-activebg="#dbdbdb"data-img=""data-newimg=""><div  class="ult_exp_section-main ">
					<div class="ult_expheader" >Pikes Peak Regional Building Department Board of Review
					 </div></div>
				</div><div class="ult_exp_content " style="background-color:#dbdbdb;  "><div class="ult_ecpsub_cont" style=" " ><section class="vc_cta3-container"><div class="vc_general vc_do_cta3 vc_cta3 vc_cta3-style-classic vc_cta3-shape-rounded vc_cta3-align-left vc_cta3-color-classic vc_cta3-icon-size-md vc_cta3-actions-bottom vc_custom_1781886102048"><div class="vc_cta3_content-container"><div class="vc_cta3-content"><header class="vc_cta3-content-header"></header><p><span style="color: #002d5d">The Pikes Peak Regional Building Department (PPRBD) Board of Review is authorized to propose standards and interpretations of the building code; to grant or deny minor variances to code; to grant, suspend or revoke contractor licenses; and impose restrictions or requirements on contractors. The board is comprised of an architect, citizen-at-large, building contractor (A or B license), building contractor (A, B or C license), and engineer (structural, electrical or mechanical).</span></p>
</div><div class="vc_cta3-actions"><div class="vc_btn3-container vc_btn3-inline" ><a class="vc_general vc_btn3 vc_btn3-size-md vc_btn3-shape-rounded vc_btn3-style-modern vc_btn3-color-grey" href="http://bocc.elpasoco.com/volunteer/city-county-board-review/" title="PPRBD">Learn more about PPRBD</a></div></div></div></div></section></div></div>

			</div></div></div></div></div><div class="vc_row wpb_row vc_row-fluid"><div class="wpb_column vc_column_container vc_col-sm-12"><div class="vc_column-inner"><div class="wpb_wrapper"><h3 style="font-size: 30px;color: #002D5D;text-align: left;font-family:Open Sans;font-weight:400;font-style:normal" class="vc_custom_heading vc_do_custom_heading" >Active Advisory Boards</h3></div></div></div></div><div class="vc_row wpb_row vc_row-fluid vc_custom_1781538141035 vc_column-gap-30"><div class="wpb_column vc_column_container vc_col-sm-6"><div class="vc_column-inner"><div class="wpb_wrapper"><div class="ult_exp_section_layer ult-adjust-bottom-margin  " >
		<div id="uvc-exp-wrap-4720" role="button" tabindex="0" aria-pressed="false"  data-ultimate-target='#uvc-exp-wrap-4720'  data-responsive-json-new='{"font-size":"desktop:20px;","line-height":"desktop:20px;"}'  class="ult_exp_section  ult-responsive " style="color:#333333;background-color:#dbdbdb; font-weight:normal;  text-align:center;" data-textcolor="#333333"data-texthover="#333333"data-icncolor="#333333"data-ihover="#333333"data-height="0"data-cntbg="#dbdbdb"data-cnthvrbg="#e5e5e5"data-headerbg="#dbdbdb"data-headerhover="#e5e5e5"data-title="City/County Drainage Board"data-newtitle="City/County Drainage Board"data-icon=""data-newicon=""data-activeicon="#333333"data-effect="slideToggle"data-override="0"data-activetitle="#333333"data-activebg="#dbdbdb"data-img=""data-newimg=""><div  class="ult_exp_section-main ">
					<div class="ult_expheader" >City/County Drainage Board
					 </div></div>
				</div><div class="ult_exp_content " style="background-color:#dbdbdb;  "><div class="ult_ecpsub_cont" style=" " ><section class="vc_cta3-container"><div class="vc_general vc_do_cta3 vc_cta3 vc_cta3-style-classic vc_cta3-shape-rounded vc_cta3-align-left vc_cta3-color-classic vc_cta3-icon-size-md vc_cta3-actions-bottom vc_custom_1781886186343"><div class="vc_cta3_content-container"><div class="vc_cta3-content"><header class="vc_cta3-content-header"></header><p><span style="color: #002d5d">The City/County Drainage Board acts as an advisory board to the Colorado Springs City Council and the Board of El Paso County Commissioners regarding (1) subdivision codes and regulations relating to the drainage and control of flood and surface waters and (2) administration of the Subdivision Storm Drainage funds. The board also works closely with the City Engineer and the County Engineer to make recommendations on new drainage studies and fees.</span></p>
</div><div class="vc_cta3-actions"><div class="vc_btn3-container vc_btn3-inline" ><a class="vc_general vc_btn3 vc_btn3-size-md vc_btn3-shape-rounded vc_btn3-style-modern vc_btn3-color-grey" href="http://bocc.elpasoco.com/volunteer/city-county-drainage-board/" title="City/County Drainage Board">City/County Drainage Board</a></div></div></div></div></section></div></div>

			</div><div class="ult_exp_section_layer ult-adjust-bottom-margin  " >
		<div id="uvc-exp-wrap-6777" role="button" tabindex="0" aria-pressed="false"  data-ultimate-target='#uvc-exp-wrap-6777'  data-responsive-json-new='{"font-size":"desktop:20px;","line-height":"desktop:20px;"}'  class="ult_exp_section  ult-responsive " style="color:#333333;background-color:#dbdbdb; font-weight:normal;  text-align:center;" data-textcolor="#333333"data-texthover="#333333"data-icncolor="#333333"data-ihover="#333333"data-height="0"data-cntbg="#dbdbdb"data-cnthvrbg="#e5e5e5"data-headerbg="#dbdbdb"data-headerhover="#e5e5e5"data-title="Community Development Advisory Board"data-newtitle="Community Development Advisory Board"data-icon=""data-newicon=""data-activeicon="#333333"data-effect="slideToggle"data-override="0"data-activetitle="#333333"data-activebg="#dbdbdb"data-img=""data-newimg=""><div  class="ult_exp_section-main ">
					<div class="ult_expheader" >Community Development Advisory Board
					 </div></div>
				</div><div class="ult_exp_content " style="background-color:#dbdbdb;  "><div class="ult_ecpsub_cont" style=" " ><section class="vc_cta3-container"><div class="vc_general vc_do_cta3 vc_cta3 vc_cta3-style-classic vc_cta3-shape-rounded vc_cta3-align-left vc_cta3-color-classic vc_cta3-icon-size-md vc_cta3-actions-bottom vc_custom_1781886198866"><div class="vc_cta3_content-container"><div class="vc_cta3-content"><header class="vc_cta3-content-header"></header><p><span style="color: #002d5d">On April 1, 2009, El Paso County became an “entitlement community” and was awarded a Community Development Block Grant (CDBG) from the U.S. Department of Housing and Urban Development (HUD) to carry out a wide range of community development activities directed toward revitalizing neighborhoods, economic development, and providing improved community facilities and services.</span></p>
<p><span style="color: #002d5d">The Community Development Advisory Board (CDAB) reviews matters of importance regarding the CDBG program and makes recommendations to the Board of El Paso County Commissioners concerning community development issues and use of CDBG funds.</span></p>
</div><div class="vc_cta3-actions"><div class="vc_btn3-container vc_btn3-inline" ><a class="vc_general vc_btn3 vc_btn3-size-md vc_btn3-shape-rounded vc_btn3-style-modern vc_btn3-color-grey" href="http://bocc.elpasoco.com/volunteer/community-development-advisory-board/" title="Community Development Advisory Board">More about the Community Development Advisory Board</a></div></div></div></div></section></div></div>

			</div><div class="ult_exp_section_layer ult-adjust-bottom-margin  " >
		<div id="uvc-exp-wrap-1897" role="button" tabindex="0" aria-pressed="false"  data-ultimate-target='#uvc-exp-wrap-1897'  data-responsive-json-new='{"font-size":"desktop:20px;","line-height":"desktop:20px;"}'  class="ult_exp_section  ult-responsive " style="color:#333333;background-color:#dbdbdb; font-weight:normal;  text-align:center;" data-textcolor="#333333"data-texthover="#333333"data-icncolor="#333333"data-ihover="#333333"data-height="0"data-cntbg="#dbdbdb"data-cnthvrbg="#e5e5e5"data-headerbg="#dbdbdb"data-headerhover="#e5e5e5"data-title="Citizen Outreach Group"data-newtitle="Citizen Outreach Group"data-icon=""data-newicon=""data-activeicon="#333333"data-effect="slideToggle"data-override="0"data-activetitle="#333333"data-activebg="#dbdbdb"data-img=""data-newimg=""><div  class="ult_exp_section-main ">
					<div class="ult_expheader" >Citizen Outreach Group
					 </div></div>
				</div><div class="ult_exp_content " style="background-color:#dbdbdb;  "><div class="ult_ecpsub_cont" style=" " ><section class="vc_cta3-container"><div class="vc_general vc_do_cta3 vc_cta3 vc_cta3-style-classic vc_cta3-shape-rounded vc_cta3-align-left vc_cta3-color-classic vc_cta3-icon-size-md vc_cta3-actions-bottom vc_custom_1781886227935"><div class="vc_cta3_content-container"><div class="vc_cta3-content"><header class="vc_cta3-content-header"></header><p><span style="color: #002d5d">The County of El Paso through the El Paso County Board of County Commissioners has created the El Paso County Citizen Outreach Group to educate residents of the work and services provided by El Paso County, serve as citizen ambassadors on behalf of the organization to the public as requested by appropriately designated staff, and assess the progress or efforts of County strategic initiatives, such as the County Strategic Plan, the County’s Budget, and the activity of the public Safety tax.</span></p>
</div><div class="vc_cta3-actions"><div class="vc_btn3-container vc_btn3-inline" ><a class="vc_general vc_btn3 vc_btn3-size-md vc_btn3-shape-rounded vc_btn3-style-modern vc_btn3-color-grey" href="http://bocc.elpasoco.com/volunteer/citizens-outreach-group/" title="Citizen Outreach">More about the Citizen Outreach Group</a></div></div></div></div></section></div></div>

			</div><div class="ult_exp_section_layer ult-adjust-bottom-margin  " >
		<div id="uvc-exp-wrap-7949" role="button" tabindex="0" aria-pressed="false"  data-ultimate-target='#uvc-exp-wrap-7949'  data-responsive-json-new='{"font-size":"desktop:20px;","line-height":"desktop:20px;"}'  class="ult_exp_section  ult-responsive " style="color:#333333;background-color:#dbdbdb; font-weight:normal;  text-align:center;" data-textcolor="#333333"data-texthover="#333333"data-icncolor="#333333"data-ihover="#333333"data-height="0"data-cntbg="#dbdbdb"data-cnthvrbg="#e5e5e5"data-headerbg="#dbdbdb"data-headerhover="#e5e5e5"data-title="Community Services Block Grant Advisory Board"data-newtitle="Community Services Block Grant Advisory Board"data-icon=""data-newicon=""data-activeicon="#333333"data-effect="slideToggle"data-override="0"data-activetitle="#333333"data-activebg="#dbdbdb"data-img=""data-newimg=""><div  class="ult_exp_section-main ">
					<div class="ult_expheader" >Community Services Block Grant Advisory Board
					 </div></div>
				</div><div class="ult_exp_content " style="background-color:#dbdbdb;  "><div class="ult_ecpsub_cont" style=" " ><section class="vc_cta3-container"><div class="vc_general vc_do_cta3 vc_cta3 vc_cta3-style-classic vc_cta3-shape-rounded vc_cta3-align-left vc_cta3-color-classic vc_cta3-icon-size-md vc_cta3-actions-bottom vc_custom_1781886239977"><div class="vc_cta3_content-container"><div class="vc_cta3-content"><header class="vc_cta3-content-header"></header><p><span style="color: #002d5d">The role of the El Paso County Community Services Block Grant Advisory Board is to participate actively in the development, planning, implementation and evaluation of the Community Services Block Grant (CSBG) program in El Paso County, serving low-income communities and making recommendations to the Board of County Commissioners.</span></p>
</div><div class="vc_cta3-actions"><div class="vc_btn3-container vc_btn3-inline" ><a class="vc_general vc_btn3 vc_btn3-size-md vc_btn3-shape-rounded vc_btn3-style-modern vc_btn3-color-grey" href="http://bocc.elpasoco.com/volunteer/community-services-block-grant-advisory-board/" title="CSBG Advisory Board">CSBG Advisory Board</a></div></div></div></div></section></div></div>

			</div><div class="ult_exp_section_layer ult-adjust-bottom-margin  " >
		<div id="uvc-exp-wrap-9185" role="button" tabindex="0" aria-pressed="false"  data-ultimate-target='#uvc-exp-wrap-9185'  data-responsive-json-new='{"font-size":"desktop:20px;","line-height":"desktop:20px;"}'  class="ult_exp_section  ult-responsive " style="color:#333333;background-color:#dbdbdb; font-weight:normal;  text-align:center;" data-textcolor="#333333"data-texthover="#333333"data-icncolor="#333333"data-ihover="#333333"data-height="0"data-cntbg="#dbdbdb"data-cnthvrbg="#e5e5e5"data-headerbg="#dbdbdb"data-headerhover="#e5e5e5"data-title="CSU Extension Advisory Committee"data-newtitle="CSU Extension Advisory Committee"data-icon=""data-newicon=""data-activeicon="#333333"data-effect="slideToggle"data-override="0"data-activetitle="#333333"data-activebg="#dbdbdb"data-img=""data-newimg=""><div  class="ult_exp_section-main ">
					<div class="ult_expheader" >CSU Extension Advisory Committee
					 </div></div>
				</div><div class="ult_exp_content " style="background-color:#dbdbdb;  "><div class="ult_ecpsub_cont" style=" " ><section class="vc_cta3-container"><div class="vc_general vc_do_cta3 vc_cta3 vc_cta3-style-classic vc_cta3-shape-rounded vc_cta3-align-left vc_cta3-color-classic vc_cta3-icon-size-md vc_cta3-actions-bottom vc_custom_1781886255377"><div class="vc_cta3_content-container"><div class="vc_cta3-content"><header class="vc_cta3-content-header"></header><p><span style="color: #002d5d">The mission of the El Paso County Extension Advisory Committee is to promote, advocate, and support the Colorado State University’s Extension program in El Paso County and staff by developing and implementing a strong marketing strategy that results in educating community officials and providing information flow between county citizens and the Extension.</span></p>
</div><div class="vc_cta3-actions"><div class="vc_btn3-container vc_btn3-inline" ><a class="vc_general vc_btn3 vc_btn3-size-md vc_btn3-shape-rounded vc_btn3-style-modern vc_btn3-color-grey" href="http://bocc.elpasoco.com/volunteer/csu-extension-advisory-committee/" title="CSU Extension Advisory Committee">CSU Extension Advisory Committee</a></div></div></div></div></section></div></div>

			</div><div class="ult_exp_section_layer ult-adjust-bottom-margin  " >
		<div id="uvc-exp-wrap-5279" role="button" tabindex="0" aria-pressed="false"  data-ultimate-target='#uvc-exp-wrap-5279'  data-responsive-json-new='{"font-size":"desktop:20px;","line-height":"desktop:20px;"}'  class="ult_exp_section  ult-responsive " style="color:#333333;background-color:#dbdbdb; font-weight:normal;  text-align:center;" data-textcolor="#333333"data-texthover="#333333"data-icncolor="#333333"data-ihover="#333333"data-height="0"data-cntbg="#dbdbdb"data-cnthvrbg="#e5e5e5"data-headerbg="#dbdbdb"data-headerhover="#e5e5e5"data-title="El Paso County Fair Advisory Board"data-newtitle="El Paso County Fair Advisory Board"data-icon=""data-newicon=""data-activeicon="#333333"data-effect="slideToggle"data-override="0"data-activetitle="#333333"data-activebg="#dbdbdb"data-img=""data-newimg=""><div  class="ult_exp_section-main ">
					<div class="ult_expheader" >El Paso County Fair Advisory Board
					 </div></div>
				</div><div class="ult_exp_content " style="background-color:#dbdbdb;  "><div class="ult_ecpsub_cont" style=" " ><section class="vc_cta3-container"><div class="vc_general vc_do_cta3 vc_cta3 vc_cta3-style-classic vc_cta3-shape-rounded vc_cta3-align-left vc_cta3-color-classic vc_cta3-icon-size-md vc_cta3-actions-bottom vc_custom_1781886266796"><div class="vc_cta3_content-container"><div class="vc_cta3-content"><header class="vc_cta3-content-header"></header><p><span style="color: #002d5d">The El Paso County Fair Advisory Board assists with the development, management, programming, operation, and maintenance of the Fair and Events Complex in Calhan. Board members also help to produce the annual County Fair.</span></p>
</div><div class="vc_cta3-actions"><div class="vc_btn3-container vc_btn3-inline" ><a class="vc_general vc_btn3 vc_btn3-size-md vc_btn3-shape-rounded vc_btn3-style-modern vc_btn3-color-grey" href="http://bocc.elpasoco.com/volunteer/fair-advisory-board/" title="EPC Fair Advisory Board">El Paso County Fair Advisory Board</a></div></div></div></div></section></div></div>

			</div><div class="ult_exp_section_layer ult-adjust-bottom-margin  " >
		<div id="uvc-exp-wrap-2755" role="button" tabindex="0" aria-pressed="false"  data-ultimate-target='#uvc-exp-wrap-2755'  data-responsive-json-new='{"font-size":"desktop:20px;","line-height":"desktop:20px;"}'  class="ult_exp_section  ult-responsive " style="color:#333333;background-color:#dbdbdb; font-weight:normal;  text-align:center;" data-textcolor="#333333"data-texthover="#333333"data-icncolor="#333333"data-ihover="#333333"data-height="0"data-cntbg="#dbdbdb"data-cnthvrbg="#e5e5e5"data-headerbg="#dbdbdb"data-headerhover="#e5e5e5"data-title="El Paso County Planning Commission"data-newtitle="El Paso County Planning Commission"data-icon=""data-newicon=""data-activeicon="#333333"data-effect="slideToggle"data-override="0"data-activetitle="#333333"data-activebg="#dbdbdb"data-img=""data-newimg=""><div  class="ult_exp_section-main ">
					<div class="ult_expheader" >El Paso County Planning Commission
					 </div></div>
				</div><div class="ult_exp_content " style="background-color:#dbdbdb;  "><div class="ult_ecpsub_cont" style=" " ><section class="vc_cta3-container"><div class="vc_general vc_do_cta3 vc_cta3 vc_cta3-style-classic vc_cta3-shape-rounded vc_cta3-align-left vc_cta3-color-classic vc_cta3-icon-size-md vc_cta3-actions-bottom vc_custom_1783456946474"><div class="vc_cta3_content-container"><div class="vc_cta3-content"><header class="vc_cta3-content-header"></header><p><span style="color: #002d5d">The Board of County Commissioners (BoCC) shall appoint a Planning Commission. The Planning Commission is established by resolution of the BoCC pursuant to C.R.S. §30-28-103 and C.R.S. §30-28-104 . The Planning Commission reviews planning petitions and makes recommendations to the Board of County Commissioners on land use requests and prepares a master plan for unincorporated areas of the county.</span></p>
</div><div class="vc_cta3-actions"><div class="vc_btn3-container vc_btn3-inline" ><a class="vc_general vc_btn3 vc_btn3-size-md vc_btn3-shape-rounded vc_btn3-style-modern vc_btn3-color-grey" href="https://planningdevelopment.elpasoco.com/planning-commission/" title="El Paso County Planning Commission">Explore more about the EPC Planning Commission</a></div></div></div></div></section></div></div>

			</div><div class="ult_exp_section_layer ult-adjust-bottom-margin  " >
		<div id="uvc-exp-wrap-5309" role="button" tabindex="0" aria-pressed="false"  data-ultimate-target='#uvc-exp-wrap-5309'  data-responsive-json-new='{"font-size":"desktop:20px;","line-height":"desktop:20px;"}'  class="ult_exp_section  ult-responsive " style="color:#333333;background-color:#dbdbdb; font-weight:normal;  text-align:center;" data-textcolor="#333333"data-texthover="#333333"data-icncolor="#333333"data-ihover="#333333"data-height="0"data-cntbg="#dbdbdb"data-cnthvrbg="#e5e5e5"data-headerbg="#dbdbdb"data-headerhover="#e5e5e5"data-title="Local Emergency Planning Committee"data-newtitle="Local Emergency Planning Committee"data-icon=""data-newicon=""data-activeicon="#333333"data-effect="slideToggle"data-override="0"data-activetitle="#333333"data-activebg="#dbdbdb"data-img=""data-newimg=""><div  class="ult_exp_section-main ">
					<div class="ult_expheader" >Local Emergency Planning Committee
					 </div></div>
				</div><div class="ult_exp_content " style="background-color:#dbdbdb;  "><div class="ult_ecpsub_cont" style=" " ><section class="vc_cta3-container"><div class="vc_general vc_do_cta3 vc_cta3 vc_cta3-style-classic vc_cta3-shape-rounded vc_cta3-align-left vc_cta3-color-classic vc_cta3-icon-size-md vc_cta3-actions-bottom vc_custom_1781886308899"><div class="vc_cta3_content-container"><div class="vc_cta3-content"><header class="vc_cta3-content-header"></header><p><span style="color: #002d5d">The Board of County Commissioners established the Local Emergency Planning Committee (LEPC) for the administration of a federal program for the development and review of chemical emergency response plans, collecting information about corporate and public use and storage of hazardous chemicals to help Fire and HAZMAT officers to safely respond to an incident, and to help citizens exercise their rights under the Federal Emergency Planning and Community Right to Know Act.</span></p>
<p><span style="color: #002d5d">Visit the Local Emergency Planning Committee website for further information. </span></p>
</div><div class="vc_cta3-actions"><div class="vc_btn3-container vc_btn3-inline" ><a class="vc_general vc_btn3 vc_btn3-size-md vc_btn3-shape-rounded vc_btn3-style-modern vc_btn3-color-grey" href="http://bocc.elpasoco.com/volunteer/local-emergency-planning-committee/" title="Local Emergency Planning Committee">Local Emergency Planning Committee</a></div></div></div></div></section></div></div>

			</div><div class="ult_exp_section_layer ult-adjust-bottom-margin  " >
		<div id="uvc-exp-wrap-2044" role="button" tabindex="0" aria-pressed="false"  data-ultimate-target='#uvc-exp-wrap-2044'  data-responsive-json-new='{"font-size":"desktop:20px;","line-height":"desktop:20px;"}'  class="ult_exp_section  ult-responsive " style="color:#333333;background-color:#dbdbdb; font-weight:normal;  text-align:center;" data-textcolor="#333333"data-texthover="#333333"data-icncolor="#333333"data-ihover="#333333"data-height="0"data-cntbg="#dbdbdb"data-cnthvrbg="#e5e5e5"data-headerbg="#dbdbdb"data-headerhover="#e5e5e5"data-title="Noxious Weed Advisory Commission"data-newtitle="Noxious Weed Advisory Commission"data-icon=""data-newicon=""data-activeicon="#333333"data-effect="slideToggle"data-override="0"data-activetitle="#333333"data-activebg="#dbdbdb"data-img=""data-newimg=""><div  class="ult_exp_section-main ">
					<div class="ult_expheader" >Noxious Weed Advisory Commission
					 </div></div>
				</div><div class="ult_exp_content " style="background-color:#dbdbdb;  "><div class="ult_ecpsub_cont" style=" " ><section class="vc_cta3-container"><div class="vc_general vc_do_cta3 vc_cta3 vc_cta3-style-classic vc_cta3-shape-rounded vc_cta3-align-left vc_cta3-color-classic vc_cta3-icon-size-md vc_cta3-actions-bottom vc_custom_1781886320621"><div class="vc_cta3_content-container"><div class="vc_cta3-content"><header class="vc_cta3-content-header"></header><p><span style="color: #002d5d">The Noxious Weed Advisory Commission develops and tri-annually reviews an action plan for the integrated management of state-mandated weeds; designates additional weeds that are or have the potential for becoming problematic in the county; and recommends to the Board of County Commissioners that identified individual landowners be required to submit their management strategies to control targeted plants to the El Paso County Environmental Division.</span></p>
<p><span style="color: #002d5d">Additionally, the Commission serves to educate the public by speaking to groups and homeowner associations and by displaying educational materials at community events.</span></p>
</div><div class="vc_cta3-actions"><div class="vc_btn3-container vc_btn3-inline" ><a class="vc_general vc_btn3 vc_btn3-size-md vc_btn3-shape-rounded vc_btn3-style-modern vc_btn3-color-grey" href="http://bocc.elpasoco.com/volunteer/noxious-weed-advisory-commission/" title="Noxious Weed Advisory Commission">More about the Noxious Weed Advisory Commission</a></div></div></div></div></section></div></div>

			</div><div class="ult_exp_section_layer ult-adjust-bottom-margin  " >
		<div id="uvc-exp-wrap-7942" role="button" tabindex="0" aria-pressed="false"  data-ultimate-target='#uvc-exp-wrap-7942'  data-responsive-json-new='{"font-size":"desktop:20px;","line-height":"desktop:20px;"}'  class="ult_exp_section  ult-responsive " style="color:#333333;background-color:#dbdbdb; font-weight:normal;  text-align:center;" data-textcolor="#333333"data-texthover="#333333"data-icncolor="#333333"data-ihover="#333333"data-height="0"data-cntbg="#dbdbdb"data-cnthvrbg="#e5e5e5"data-headerbg="#dbdbdb"data-headerhover="#e5e5e5"data-title="Park Advisory Board"data-newtitle="Park Advisory Board"data-icon=""data-newicon=""data-activeicon="#333333"data-effect="slideToggle"data-override="0"data-activetitle="#333333"data-activebg="#dbdbdb"data-img=""data-newimg=""><div  class="ult_exp_section-main ">
					<div class="ult_expheader" >Park Advisory Board
					 </div></div>
				</div><div class="ult_exp_content " style="background-color:#dbdbdb;  "><div class="ult_ecpsub_cont" style=" " ><section class="vc_cta3-container"><div class="vc_general vc_do_cta3 vc_cta3 vc_cta3-style-classic vc_cta3-shape-rounded vc_cta3-align-left vc_cta3-color-classic vc_cta3-icon-size-md vc_cta3-actions-bottom vc_custom_1781886332271"><div class="vc_cta3_content-container"><div class="vc_cta3-content"><header class="vc_cta3-content-header"></header><p><span style="color: #002d5d">The Park Advisory Board reviews and comments on items and proposals related to County Park policies, philosophies and objectives, and makes recommendations to the Board of County Commissioners.</span></p>
</div><div class="vc_cta3-actions"><div class="vc_btn3-container vc_btn3-inline" ><a class="vc_general vc_btn3 vc_btn3-size-md vc_btn3-shape-rounded vc_btn3-style-modern vc_btn3-color-grey" href="http://bocc.elpasoco.com/volunteer/park-advisory-board/" title="Parks Advisory Board">More about the Parks Advisory Board</a></div></div></div></div></section></div></div>

			</div></div></div></div><div class="wpb_column vc_column_container vc_col-sm-6"><div class="vc_column-inner"><div class="wpb_wrapper"><div class="ult_exp_section_layer ult-adjust-bottom-margin  " >
		<div id="uvc-exp-wrap-9989" role="button" tabindex="0" aria-pressed="false"  data-ultimate-target='#uvc-exp-wrap-9989'  data-responsive-json-new='{"font-size":"desktop:20px;","line-height":"desktop:20px;"}'  class="ult_exp_section  ult-responsive " style="color:#333333;background-color:#dbdbdb; font-weight:normal;  text-align:center;" data-textcolor="#333333"data-texthover="#333333"data-icncolor="#333333"data-ihover="#333333"data-height="0"data-cntbg="#dbdbdb"data-cnthvrbg="#e5e5e5"data-headerbg="#dbdbdb"data-headerhover="#e5e5e5"data-title="Pikes Peak Area Council of Governments - Area Agency on Aging"data-newtitle="Pikes Peak Area Council of Governments - Area Agency on Aging"data-icon=""data-newicon=""data-activeicon="#333333"data-effect="slideToggle"data-override="0"data-activetitle="#333333"data-activebg="#dbdbdb"data-img=""data-newimg=""><div  class="ult_exp_section-main ">
					<div class="ult_expheader" >Pikes Peak Area Council of Governments - Area Agency on Aging
					 </div></div>
				</div><div class="ult_exp_content " style="background-color:#dbdbdb;  "><div class="ult_ecpsub_cont" style=" " ><section class="vc_cta3-container"><div class="vc_general vc_do_cta3 vc_cta3 vc_cta3-style-classic vc_cta3-shape-rounded vc_cta3-align-left vc_cta3-color-classic vc_cta3-icon-size-md vc_cta3-actions-bottom vc_custom_1781886494721"><div class="vc_cta3_content-container"><div class="vc_cta3-content"><header class="vc_cta3-content-header"></header><p><span style="color: #002d5d">The purpose of the Commission is to advise and recommend to the PPACG Board of Directors and PPACG staff action on matters regarding the development of an area-wide system of advocacy and policy recommendations for older persons to enable them to maintain as much independence as possible.</span></p>
</div><div class="vc_cta3-actions"><div class="vc_btn3-container vc_btn3-inline" ><a class="vc_general vc_btn3 vc_btn3-size-md vc_btn3-shape-rounded vc_btn3-style-modern vc_btn3-color-grey" href="http://bocc.elpasoco.com/volunteer/pikes-peak-agency-aging-regional-advisory-council/" title="Piles Peak Agency on Aging ">Learn more about Pikes Peak Agency on Aging</a></div></div></div></div></section></div></div>

			</div><div class="ult_exp_section_layer ult-adjust-bottom-margin  " >
		<div id="uvc-exp-wrap-9349" role="button" tabindex="0" aria-pressed="false"  data-ultimate-target='#uvc-exp-wrap-9349'  data-responsive-json-new='{"font-size":"desktop:20px;","line-height":"desktop:20px;"}'  class="ult_exp_section  ult-responsive " style="color:#333333;background-color:#dbdbdb; font-weight:normal;  text-align:center;" data-textcolor="#333333"data-texthover="#333333"data-icncolor="#333333"data-ihover="#333333"data-height="0"data-cntbg="#dbdbdb"data-cnthvrbg="#e5e5e5"data-headerbg="#dbdbdb"data-headerhover="#e5e5e5"data-title="Pikes Peak Area Council of Governments Community Advisory Committee"data-newtitle="Pikes Peak Area Council of Governments Community Advisory Committee"data-icon=""data-newicon=""data-activeicon="#333333"data-effect="slideToggle"data-override="0"data-activetitle="#333333"data-activebg="#dbdbdb"data-img=""data-newimg=""><div  class="ult_exp_section-main ">
					<div class="ult_expheader" >Pikes Peak Area Council of Governments Community Advisory Committee
					 </div></div>
				</div><div class="ult_exp_content " style="background-color:#dbdbdb;  "><div class="ult_ecpsub_cont" style=" " ><section class="vc_cta3-container"><div class="vc_general vc_do_cta3 vc_cta3 vc_cta3-style-classic vc_cta3-shape-rounded vc_cta3-align-left vc_cta3-color-classic vc_cta3-icon-size-md vc_cta3-actions-bottom vc_custom_1781886483038"><div class="vc_cta3_content-container"><div class="vc_cta3-content"><header class="vc_cta3-content-header"></header><p><span style="color: #002d5d">The Pikes Peak Area Council of Governments (PPACG) Community Advisory Committee (CAC) was formed to afford citizens the opportunity to be continuously involved in regional planning activities. The CAC is an advisory committee to the PPACG Board of Directors on matters affecting regional transportation, air and water quality, and military impact planning.</span></p>
</div><div class="vc_cta3-actions"><div class="vc_btn3-container vc_btn3-inline" ><a class="vc_general vc_btn3 vc_btn3-size-md vc_btn3-shape-rounded vc_btn3-style-modern vc_btn3-color-grey" href="https://bocc.elpasoco.com/volunteer/pikes-peak-area-council-governments-community-advisory-committee/" title="Community Advisory Committee">More about the Community Advisory Committee</a></div></div></div></div></section></div></div>

			</div><div class="ult_exp_section_layer ult-adjust-bottom-margin  " >
		<div id="uvc-exp-wrap-8212" role="button" tabindex="0" aria-pressed="false"  data-ultimate-target='#uvc-exp-wrap-8212'  data-responsive-json-new='{"font-size":"desktop:20px;","line-height":"desktop:20px;"}'  class="ult_exp_section  ult-responsive " style="color:#333333;background-color:#dbdbdb; font-weight:normal;  text-align:center;" data-textcolor="#333333"data-texthover="#333333"data-icncolor="#333333"data-ihover="#333333"data-height="0"data-cntbg="#dbdbdb"data-cnthvrbg="#e5e5e5"data-headerbg="#dbdbdb"data-headerhover="#e5e5e5"data-title="Pikes Peak Regional Building Department Licensing Committee"data-newtitle="Pikes Peak Regional Building Department Licensing Committee"data-icon=""data-newicon=""data-activeicon="#333333"data-effect="slideToggle"data-override="0"data-activetitle="#333333"data-activebg="#dbdbdb"data-img=""data-newimg=""><div  class="ult_exp_section-main ">
					<div class="ult_expheader" >Pikes Peak Regional Building Department Licensing Committee
					 </div></div>
				</div><div class="ult_exp_content " style="background-color:#dbdbdb;  "><div class="ult_ecpsub_cont" style=" " ><section class="vc_cta3-container"><div class="vc_general vc_do_cta3 vc_cta3 vc_cta3-style-classic vc_cta3-shape-rounded vc_cta3-align-left vc_cta3-color-classic vc_cta3-icon-size-md vc_cta3-actions-bottom vc_custom_1781886411672"><div class="vc_cta3_content-container"><div class="vc_cta3-content"><header class="vc_cta3-content-header"></header><p><span style="color: #002d5d">The Licensing Committee reviews testing, experience and licensing of applicants for licenses and the performance of work required under the Pikes Peak Regional Building Code and adopted primary and secondary codes by reference, including, but not limited to the Elevator and Escalator Safety Code. Electrical and plumbing contractors are licensed by the State of Colorado, but must also register with Pikes Peak Regional Building Department to perform work in this Jurisdiction. The committee also hears complaints against contractors.</span></p>
</div><div class="vc_cta3-actions"><div class="vc_btn3-container vc_btn3-inline" ><a class="vc_general vc_btn3 vc_btn3-size-md vc_btn3-shape-rounded vc_btn3-style-modern vc_btn3-color-grey" href="http://bocc.elpasoco.com/volunteer/pikes-peak-regional-building-department-licensing-committee/" title="Licensing Committee">More about the Licensing Committee</a></div></div></div></div></section></div></div>

			</div><div class="ult_exp_section_layer ult-adjust-bottom-margin  " >
		<div id="uvc-exp-wrap-8512" role="button" tabindex="0" aria-pressed="false"  data-ultimate-target='#uvc-exp-wrap-8512'  data-responsive-json-new='{"font-size":"desktop:20px;","line-height":"desktop:20px;"}'  class="ult_exp_section  ult-responsive " style="color:#333333;background-color:#dbdbdb; font-weight:normal;  text-align:center;" data-textcolor="#333333"data-texthover="#333333"data-icncolor="#333333"data-ihover="#333333"data-height="0"data-cntbg="#dbdbdb"data-cnthvrbg="#e5e5e5"data-headerbg="#dbdbdb"data-headerhover="#e5e5e5"data-title="Pikes Peak Regional Building Department Technical Committee"data-newtitle="Pikes Peak Regional Building Department Technical Committee"data-icon=""data-newicon=""data-activeicon="#333333"data-effect="slideToggle"data-override="0"data-activetitle="#333333"data-activebg="#dbdbdb"data-img=""data-newimg=""><div  class="ult_exp_section-main ">
					<div class="ult_expheader" >Pikes Peak Regional Building Department Technical Committee
					 </div></div>
				</div><div class="ult_exp_content " style="background-color:#dbdbdb;  "><div class="ult_ecpsub_cont" style=" " ><section class="vc_cta3-container"><div class="vc_general vc_do_cta3 vc_cta3 vc_cta3-style-classic vc_cta3-shape-rounded vc_cta3-align-left vc_cta3-color-classic vc_cta3-icon-size-md vc_cta3-actions-bottom vc_custom_1781886401013"><div class="vc_cta3_content-container"><div class="vc_cta3-content"><header class="vc_cta3-content-header"></header><p><span style="color: #002d5d">The Technical Committee reviews, interprets, and recommends minor variance requests from the Pikes Peak Regional Building Code (the “Building Code”), including, but not limited to the Sign Code, and the Elevator and Escalator Safety Code.</span></p>
</div><div class="vc_cta3-actions"><div class="vc_btn3-container vc_btn3-inline" ><a class="vc_general vc_btn3 vc_btn3-size-md vc_btn3-shape-rounded vc_btn3-style-modern vc_btn3-color-grey" href="http://bocc.elpasoco.com/volunteer/pikes-peak-regional-building-department-technical-committee/" title="Technical Committee">More about the Technical Committee</a></div></div></div></div></section></div></div>

			</div><div class="ult_exp_section_layer ult-adjust-bottom-margin  " >
		<div id="uvc-exp-wrap-1264" role="button" tabindex="0" aria-pressed="false"  data-ultimate-target='#uvc-exp-wrap-1264'  data-responsive-json-new='{"font-size":"desktop:20px;","line-height":"desktop:20px;"}'  class="ult_exp_section  ult-responsive " style="color:#333333;background-color:#dbdbdb; font-weight:normal;  text-align:center;" data-textcolor="#333333"data-texthover="#333333"data-icncolor="#333333"data-ihover="#333333"data-height="0"data-cntbg="#dbdbdb"data-cnthvrbg="#e5e5e5"data-headerbg="#dbdbdb"data-headerhover="#e5e5e5"data-title="Pikes Peak Regional Water Authority"data-newtitle="Pikes Peak Regional Water Authority"data-icon=""data-newicon=""data-activeicon="#333333"data-effect="slideToggle"data-override="0"data-activetitle="#333333"data-activebg="#dbdbdb"data-img=""data-newimg=""><div  class="ult_exp_section-main ">
					<div class="ult_expheader" >Pikes Peak Regional Water Authority
					 </div></div>
				</div><div class="ult_exp_content " style="background-color:#dbdbdb;  "><div class="ult_ecpsub_cont" style=" " ><section class="vc_cta3-container"><div class="vc_general vc_do_cta3 vc_cta3 vc_cta3-style-classic vc_cta3-shape-rounded vc_cta3-align-left vc_cta3-color-classic vc_cta3-icon-size-md vc_custom_1771355225449"><div class="vc_cta3_content-container"><div class="vc_cta3-content"><header class="vc_cta3-content-header"></header><p><span style="color: #002d5d">Pikes Peak Regional Water Authority (PPRWA) is governed by its members and offers levels of voting membership based on the number of taps in the organization. An executive committee is appointed each year, with chairmanship rotating among members every two years. ​​</span></p>
<p><span style="color: #002d5d">For more information, please contact the Boards and Commissions Administrator at (719) 520-6555.</span></p>
</div></div></div></section></div></div>

			</div><div class="ult_exp_section_layer ult-adjust-bottom-margin  " >
		<div id="uvc-exp-wrap-6742" role="button" tabindex="0" aria-pressed="false"  data-ultimate-target='#uvc-exp-wrap-6742'  data-responsive-json-new='{"font-size":"desktop:20px;","line-height":"desktop:20px;"}'  class="ult_exp_section  ult-responsive " style="color:#333333;background-color:#dbdbdb; font-weight:normal;  text-align:center;" data-textcolor="#333333"data-texthover="#333333"data-icncolor="#333333"data-ihover="#333333"data-height="0"data-cntbg="#dbdbdb"data-cnthvrbg="#e5e5e5"data-headerbg="#dbdbdb"data-headerhover="#e5e5e5"data-title="Pikes Peak Rural Transportation Authority Citizen Advisory Committee"data-newtitle="Pikes Peak Rural Transportation Authority Citizen Advisory Committee"data-icon=""data-newicon=""data-activeicon="#333333"data-effect="slideToggle"data-override="0"data-activetitle="#333333"data-activebg="#dbdbdb"data-img=""data-newimg=""><div  class="ult_exp_section-main ">
					<div class="ult_expheader" >Pikes Peak Rural Transportation Authority Citizen Advisory Committee
					 </div></div>
				</div><div class="ult_exp_content " style="background-color:#dbdbdb;  "><div class="ult_ecpsub_cont" style=" " ><section class="vc_cta3-container"><div class="vc_general vc_do_cta3 vc_cta3 vc_cta3-style-classic vc_cta3-shape-rounded vc_cta3-align-left vc_cta3-color-classic vc_cta3-icon-size-md vc_cta3-actions-bottom vc_custom_1781886382213"><div class="vc_cta3_content-container"><div class="vc_cta3-content"><header class="vc_cta3-content-header"></header><p><span style="color: #002d5d">The Pikes Peak Rural Transportation Authority (PPRTA) is a collaborative effort among six regional governments to improve and maintain roads and support public transit. The members of PPRTA are the cities of Colorado Springs and Manitou Springs, El Paso County, and the towns of Green Mountain Falls and Ramah and Calhan.</span></p>
</div><div class="vc_cta3-actions"><div class="vc_btn3-container vc_btn3-inline" ><a class="vc_general vc_btn3 vc_btn3-size-md vc_btn3-shape-rounded vc_btn3-style-modern vc_btn3-color-grey" href="http://bocc.elpasoco.com/volunteer/pikes-peak-area-council-governments-community-advisory-committee/" title="PPRTA">Explore more about PPRTA</a></div></div></div></div></section></div></div>

			</div><div class="ult_exp_section_layer ult-adjust-bottom-margin  " >
		<div id="uvc-exp-wrap-1646" role="button" tabindex="0" aria-pressed="false"  data-ultimate-target='#uvc-exp-wrap-1646'  data-responsive-json-new='{"font-size":"desktop:20px;","line-height":"desktop:20px;"}'  class="ult_exp_section  ult-responsive " style="color:#333333;background-color:#dbdbdb; font-weight:normal;  text-align:center;" data-textcolor="#333333"data-texthover="#333333"data-icncolor="#333333"data-ihover="#333333"data-height="0"data-cntbg="#dbdbdb"data-cnthvrbg="#e5e5e5"data-headerbg="#dbdbdb"data-headerhover="#e5e5e5"data-title="Pioneer Village Roads Public Improvement District Advisory Committee"data-newtitle="Pioneer Village Roads Public Improvement District Advisory Committee"data-icon=""data-newicon=""data-activeicon="#333333"data-effect="slideToggle"data-override="0"data-activetitle="#333333"data-activebg="#dbdbdb"data-img=""data-newimg=""><div  class="ult_exp_section-main ">
					<div class="ult_expheader" >Pioneer Village Roads Public Improvement District Advisory Committee
					 </div></div>
				</div><div class="ult_exp_content " style="background-color:#dbdbdb;  "><div class="ult_ecpsub_cont" style=" " ><section class="vc_cta3-container"><div class="vc_general vc_do_cta3 vc_cta3 vc_cta3-style-classic vc_cta3-shape-rounded vc_cta3-align-left vc_cta3-color-classic vc_cta3-icon-size-md vc_cta3-actions-bottom vc_custom_1781886370409"><div class="vc_cta3_content-container"><div class="vc_cta3-content"><header class="vc_cta3-content-header"></header><p><span style="color: #002d5d">In conjunction with the establishment of the El Paso County Pioneer Village Roads Public Improvement District, the Board of County Commissioners also created the El Paso County Pioneer Village Roads Public Improvement District Advisory Committee. The purpose of the Advisory Committee is to make recommendations to the Board of County Commissioners regarding the public improvements to be funded each year, the awarding of contracts, and the need to seek an increase of the maximum mill levy for the PID.</span></p>
</div><div class="vc_cta3-actions"><div class="vc_btn3-container vc_btn3-inline" ><a class="vc_general vc_btn3 vc_btn3-size-md vc_btn3-shape-rounded vc_btn3-style-modern vc_btn3-color-grey" href="http://bocc.elpasoco.com/volunteer/pioneer-village-roads-public-improvement-district-advisory-committee/" title="Public Improvement District">More on the Public Improvement District</a></div></div></div></div></section></div></div>

			</div><div class="ult_exp_section_layer ult-adjust-bottom-margin  " >
		<div id="uvc-exp-wrap-7438" role="button" tabindex="0" aria-pressed="false"  data-ultimate-target='#uvc-exp-wrap-7438'  data-responsive-json-new='{"font-size":"desktop:20px;","line-height":"desktop:20px;"}'  class="ult_exp_section  ult-responsive " style="color:#333333;background-color:#dbdbdb; font-weight:normal;  text-align:center;" data-textcolor="#333333"data-texthover="#333333"data-icncolor="#333333"data-ihover="#333333"data-height="0"data-cntbg="#dbdbdb"data-cnthvrbg="#e5e5e5"data-headerbg="#dbdbdb"data-headerhover="#e5e5e5"data-title="Road Impact Fee Advisory Committee"data-newtitle="Road Impact Fee Advisory Committee"data-icon=""data-newicon=""data-activeicon="#333333"data-effect="slideToggle"data-override="0"data-activetitle="#333333"data-activebg="#dbdbdb"data-img=""data-newimg=""><div  class="ult_exp_section-main ">
					<div class="ult_expheader" >Road Impact Fee Advisory Committee
					 </div></div>
				</div><div class="ult_exp_content " style="background-color:#dbdbdb;  "><div class="ult_ecpsub_cont" style=" " ><section class="vc_cta3-container"><div class="vc_general vc_do_cta3 vc_cta3 vc_cta3-style-classic vc_cta3-shape-rounded vc_cta3-align-left vc_cta3-color-classic vc_cta3-icon-size-md vc_cta3-actions-bottom vc_custom_1781886356791"><div class="vc_cta3_content-container"><div class="vc_cta3-content"><header class="vc_cta3-content-header"></header><p><span style="color: #002d5d">The Committee was created by the El Paso County Planning and Community Development Department and the Department of Public Works to provide recommendations to the Commissioners on the implementation of the unincorporated county-wide road impact fee program, in compliance with local, state, and federal laws.</span></p>
<p><span style="color: #002d5d">For further information, please contact the Boards and Commissions Administrator at 719-520-6555.</span></p>
</div><div class="vc_cta3-actions"><div class="vc_btn3-container vc_btn3-inline" ><a class="vc_general vc_btn3 vc_btn3-size-md vc_btn3-shape-rounded vc_btn3-style-modern vc_btn3-color-grey" href="http://bocc.elpasoco.com/volunteer/road-impact-advisory-committee/" title="Road Impact Fee Advisory Committee">Advisory Committee</a></div></div></div></div></section></div></div>

			</div><div class="ult_exp_section_layer ult-adjust-bottom-margin  " >
		<div id="uvc-exp-wrap-4100" role="button" tabindex="0" aria-pressed="false"  data-ultimate-target='#uvc-exp-wrap-4100'  data-responsive-json-new='{"font-size":"desktop:20px;","line-height":"desktop:20px;"}'  class="ult_exp_section  ult-responsive " style="color:#333333;background-color:#dbdbdb; font-weight:normal;  text-align:center;" data-textcolor="#333333"data-texthover="#333333"data-icncolor="#333333"data-ihover="#333333"data-height="0"data-cntbg="#dbdbdb"data-cnthvrbg="#e5e5e5"data-headerbg="#dbdbdb"data-headerhover="#e5e5e5"data-title="Widefield Water and Sanitation District Citizens’ Advisory Council"data-newtitle="Widefield Water and Sanitation District Citizens’ Advisory Council"data-icon=""data-newicon=""data-activeicon="#333333"data-effect="slideToggle"data-override="0"data-activetitle="#333333"data-activebg="#dbdbdb"data-img=""data-newimg=""><div  class="ult_exp_section-main ">
					<div class="ult_expheader" >Widefield Water and Sanitation District Citizens’ Advisory Council
					 </div></div>
				</div><div class="ult_exp_content " style="background-color:#dbdbdb;  "><div class="ult_ecpsub_cont" style=" " ><section class="vc_cta3-container"><div class="vc_general vc_do_cta3 vc_cta3 vc_cta3-style-classic vc_cta3-shape-rounded vc_cta3-align-left vc_cta3-color-classic vc_cta3-icon-size-md vc_cta3-actions-bottom vc_custom_1781886342524"><div class="vc_cta3_content-container"><div class="vc_cta3-content"><header class="vc_cta3-content-header"></header><p><span style="color: #002d5d">The Citizen Advisory Council is a component of the District for customer representation for citizens with the District’s boundaries and provides a point of contact for the public.</span></p>
</div><div class="vc_cta3-actions"><div class="vc_btn3-container vc_btn3-inline" ><a class="vc_general vc_btn3 vc_btn3-size-md vc_btn3-shape-rounded vc_btn3-style-modern vc_btn3-color-grey" href="http://bocc.elpasoco.com/volunteer/widefield-water-and-sanitation-district-citizens-advisory-council/" title="Citizen Advisory Council">Learn more about the Citizen Advisory Council</a></div></div></div></div></section></div></div>

			</div></div></div></div></div></section><section class="vc_section"><div class="vc_row wpb_row vc_row-fluid"><div class="wpb_column vc_column_container vc_col-sm-12"><div class="vc_column-inner"><div class="wpb_wrapper"><div class="vc_empty_space"   style="height: 32px"><span class="vc_empty_space_inner"></span></div>
	<div  class="wpb_single_image wpb_content_element vc_align_center">
		
